-# USR-10: the language of the pages, between the theme button and the
  account button. A popover, as the theme menu is; each choice is a form of
  its own, sent with a full load of the page. A language stands by its own
  name, marked as that language for a screen reader. The code on the button
  is read out with its name, so that a voice finds the button by what is seen.
%button.header-button.language-button{ type: "button", popovertarget: "language-menu" }
  = outline_icon("globe-alt", 20, class: "globe")
  %span.language-code= I18n.locale.to_s.upcase
  %span.visually-hidden= t(".button", language: Language.name_of(I18n.locale))
  = outline_icon("chevron-down", 16, class: "chevron")
.language-menu#language-menu{ popover: "auto", role: "group", aria: { label: t(".label") } }
  - Language.offered.each do |code|
    = button_to language_path, method: :patch, params: { language: code }, lang: code,
      aria: { current: ("true" if I18n.locale.to_s == code) }, form: { data: { turbo: false } } do
      = outline_icon("language", 16)
      = Language.name_of(code)
